--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -13,3 +13,19 @@ A small team notes app. Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind.
 ```bash
 npm run dev
 ```
+
+## Authentication
+
+Notely uses [Better Auth](https://better-auth.com) with email + password and Google sign-in.
+Users and sessions live in a local SQLite file (Node's built-in `node:sqlite`, so Node 22.13+ is required).
+
+```bash
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then fill in a real BETTER_AUTH_SECRET and Google credentials
+npm run db:migrate           # creates the user/session/account/verification tables
+npm run dev
+```
+
+- `/sign-up`, `/sign-in` are the auth pages; `/api/auth/*` is the Better Auth handler.
+- `/dashboard` is protected twice: `src/proxy.ts` redirects requests with no session cookie,
+  and the page itself validates the session via `getCurrentUser()` in `src/lib/users.ts`.
+- For Google, add `http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google` as an authorized redirect URI.
